  "summary": "The references use darkness as a contrast with trust, revelation, and conduct. Psalm 27 expresses confidence in the Lord as light; John 1 says darkness has not overcome the light; Ephesians 5 calls readers to leave former darkness and live as light; 1 John 1 warns against claiming fellowship with God while walking in darkness. The Hebrew psalm and Greek New Testament texts contribute related imagery, but this does not make them instances of one original-language word.",
  "historical_context": "The sources range from a psalm of confidence to a Gospel prologue and letters that exhort their readers. Their literary contexts support the comparison of images; no external historical or lexical claim is added.",
