  "literary_context": "The psalm is a prayer, John’s prologue is a theological opening, and Ephesians and 1 John give ethical exhortation. Darkness can describe danger, opposition, or a life inconsistent with truth in these settings. The references should be read in their own arguments rather than as a fixed code.",
  "covenantal_significance": "The passages contrast God’s light with danger or conduct incompatible with fellowship. They link trust in God with truthful, changed living, while each writer applies the image differently.",
